  "brief": "Low one-storey stone farmhouse built 1899 of squared pale buff stone blocks, under a broad hipped roof of dark grey asphalt shingle with deep eaves, tall one-over-one windows in dark frames and a small gabled frame porch at the east end. A later one-storey frame wing in pale lap siding with a big picture window extends the west end. It sits deep in the shade of huge old cottonwoods behind a low wire-and-iron yard fence, with a white gambrel barn, a grey metal machine shed and small white garages spread across the grass beyond. (Hipped one-storey stone cottage; nearest archetype is workers_cottage.)",
